WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.710
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.180
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.920
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.840
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.470
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.600
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.700
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.740
Morning!

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.090
Good morning!

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.020
Morning, Kazuya-kun.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.000
Morning, Mikage-san.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:11.050
I’ll help you. Yamada-san is in 202, Sasaki-san is…

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:14.500
I’m OK. I’ve remembered them all.{?}

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.600
Really?

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.520
Hey, Kazuya-kun, why are you working part-time?

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.140
What?

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.610
Does your family not give you an allowance?

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.640
Isn’t your family rich?

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.260
Not really,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.300
we’re normal. Newspaper delivery is…

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.890
See, it’s also good training.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:46.770
That’s right, since you’re one of the
 potential marathon winners.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.750
Yeah. Well, later.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:13.960
The Goldfish in the Mirror

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.970
Yuurisan-Subs & マイワイフ Subs

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.970
http://yuurisan-subs.org
http://maiwaifufansubs.wordpress.com

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.970
Sub Dedicated to Enma Ai

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:49.280
This program is made possible by Sony Music,

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.920
and the listed sponsors.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.250
Oh, Kazuya.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.860
For once,

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.240
maybe we should walk together for a bit?

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.060
Here, dear. Did you forget anything?

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.350
You’ve grown.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.830
Dear, can you return early tonight?

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.600
I’m leaving.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:20.030
Kazuya! Wait!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.600
Hey, dear, tonight…

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.680
I’m busy, I have no idea.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.440
But you’ve been late recently; for once…

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.390
I’m telling you I have no idea!

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.140
Kazuya.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.570
Buy some new shoes with this money.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.860
You’re competition’s soon, right?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.840
Thanks.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:49.090
I was good at marathons, too, you
 know. Yes, the feeling was…

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.730
It was tough, but I worked hard.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.730
I’m OK!

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.420
But…

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.960
Do it with confidence!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.130
Good luck at work, dear! {itterasshai}

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.560
Good luck! {itterasshai}

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:05.200
Hey, that’s the first grader Ichimura
 Kazuya’s mother, right?

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.090
So flamboyant this early!

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:18.630
<i>TL Note: nursery song “The Goldfish’s Nap.”</i>

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:18.630
<i>Cute goldfish, wearing a red kimono.</i>

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:26.320
<i>If you wake up, I’ll make you a feast.</i>

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:33.370
<i>The red goldfish lets out a bubble.</i>

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:41.560
<i>Dozing off, it wakes from its dream.</i>

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
OK! Two more laps!

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.050
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.400
Ichimura-kun, good timing! Keep it up!

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.080
Yes!

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:59.350
Hey, you’re slowing down!

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.440
Sensei, forgive us!

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.840
It’s too much! It’s hell!

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:11.020
What’re you saying? Real Hell is much worse!

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.930
Oni! Devil!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.570
Work hard! One more lap!

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:16.030
Ouch!

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.300
At least call me the Great King Enma.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.530
That must be sadism.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.160
Are you being frustrated?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:25.820
Huh?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.180
Oh, next class! Next class!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:35.340
Sadist, sadist, always!

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.850
Same as always.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:50.580
Yeah, he’s carrying the doll around, ambivalent about pulling the string.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.500
I bet he’s scared.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:54.470
Scared?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:59.070
If he pulls the string, he himself will eventually fall to Hell.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.970
Knowing what his destination is like.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:07.100
Does he still want to send someone to Hell?

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:20.840
I’m home.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:30.610
This is beautiful!

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.620
But maybe too flashy?

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:36.210
Not at all!

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:40.120
It still suits you very well, ma’am.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.380
You look very nice since you’re so young.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.080
You’re good at words, aren’t you?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:49.560
If you wear this, your husband will
 fall in love all over again!

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.480
Really?

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.330
I wonder…

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.960
Of course.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.440
I’m jealous of your husband!

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:02.950
Oh, Kazuya, welcome home!

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:07.350
Which one do you prefer?

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:09.620
Didn’t you just buy one?

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.700
Oh, but that was for the spring!

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.140
This is separate; it’s a formal summer kimono!

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.000
Both suit you very well.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.610
Right, kid?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.250
Really?

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.350
I’m lost!

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.100
Both suit you very well.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:53.060
How about if you buy both, I give you a discount?

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.440
But…

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:58.960
If you’re unsure about payment,
 you can use a loan like always.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.520
It’s only a small amount per month.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:04.080
Well…

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.310
This kimono is also very happy.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.940
Being worn by a beautiful lady such as yourself.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.550
Oh, really?

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.070
Yes.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:21.960
Am I, beautiful?

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.450
So beautiful.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:25.280
Really?

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.810
OK, I’ll take both.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.280
Thank you very much.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:44.290
<i>Am I, beautiful?</i>

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.800
I’ve finished with the evening paper.

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:51.880
You must be tired. Already finished?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.190
You’re always so quick.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.340
Here, this month’s wages.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:57.760
Thanks a lot!

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.180
Thank you very much.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.030
Kazuya-kun.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.480
Oh.

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:07.690
Good evening.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:12.300
I wish I could work part time!

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:16.940
But, my parents would get mad if I don’t study.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:22.930
Do your parents get along well?

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:27.880
I don’t know since I’m separated,

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.500
but I don’t think they get along badly.

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:33.890
How about your parents, Kazuya-kun?

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:55.270
So you bought it after all.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.180
Does it suit me?

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:03.190
This color suits me; he said it was mother-like.

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:06.920
Don’t let him in the house anymore!

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.100
Why? He’s a nice person!

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.480
I hate him!

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.030
I’m home.

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.220
It’s your father!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.600
Welcome home!

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:27.490
How does this look, dear?

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.690
What’s with all these kimono?

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.210
You don’t like it?

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.190
Isn’t it beautiful?

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.550
Where’s dinner?

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:37.630
What?

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.420
I’m asking where’s my dinner! Aren’t you the mother of this household?

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.000
Is a mother not a woman anymore?

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.530
What’re you saying?

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:52.890
Fine, I’m eating out.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.970
Kazuya, let’s go.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.600
I’m fine.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.440
Do what you like!

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:08.530
<i>Cute goldfish, wearing a red kimono.</i>

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:10.250
<i>How pretty!</i>

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.180
<i>How pretty!</i>

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:14.790
Dear!

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.270
Saito-san!

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:25.120
Oh, ma’am! You’ve already worn it? How beautiful!

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:30.300
There was an omission on a form.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.930
Oh!

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:36.720
I have an obi that would fit that
 kimono perfectly in my car!

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.320
Just a glance, perhaps?

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:40.320
I’ll take it.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.200
Are you sure?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.200
Yes, of course.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:49.850
My husband is willing to buy as much as I want to keep me beautiful.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.600
You sure are loved!

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:55.980
Yes, I’m loved!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:58.750
Well, I’ll bring it immediately.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.620
<i>If only he weren’t here.</i>

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:17.750
Saito Yukihiro

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:22.010
Send

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:18.500
 m 0 -6 l 0 -10 l 15 -8 l 15 -5 l 15 -5  

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:18.500
Saito Yukihiro

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:22.010
Saito Yukihiro

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:30.850
Saito Yukihiro

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:30.850
Send

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:32.610
I’m here.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.120
Yamawaro.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.230
Yes, Ojou.

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:49.130
Take this.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:58.330
If you really want to curse someone…

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.690
Pull that red string.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:07.300
If you pull it, it would signify a formal agreeement with me.

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:13.560
They will swiftly be sent to Hell.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:20.490
But if you do, you must pay the price.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.400
Curse someone, and two holes are created.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:27.870
Agree, and your soul will fall to Hell.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:33.240
That’s after you die, though.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:37.530
The rest is up to you.

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.240
No, Kazuya-kun!

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.190
Stop!

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:28.700
How long will he support his mother?

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:36.250
He hates the company that sells his mother kimono, but he’s scared of Hell.

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:39.840
That mother’s old, so…

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:43.970
Women are women no matter how old.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.650
You guys probably don’t understand.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:57.410
Mom, I have a marathon today,
 so I need a change of clothes.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:02.400
Morning! Hey Kazuya, listen, listen!

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:03.780
What happened?

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:08.830
Dad was saying that, but he understands!

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:09.740
Oh, really.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:15.350
He left some money in my wallet during the night! I guess I’ll buy that pink kimono, too!

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:19.880
Really?

